      en: "The Banjul Old Cathedral, officially the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Immaculate Conception, was completed in 1916 and stands as a prime example of neo-Gothic architecture in West Africa. It served as the spiritual center for British settlers during the colonial era and was later elevated to the cathedral of the Roman Catholic Diocese of Banjul. Constructed from local stone and imported materials, the building reflects European architectural influences. After several renovations, most recently in 2005, it remains a key cultural heritage site in The Gambia.",
